@!internal

--[[
`io.net.internal.contracts` defines the network transport contract.

```nupp:fragment
local contract = io.net.internal.contracts
local type Provider = contract.Provider
```


Importing this declaration opens no sockets. The facade retains the provider
table and supplies it as the explicit receiver for every operation. Provider
handles are opaque; shared Address values come from [](io.net.Address).

Listener acceptance, connection completion, and stream I/O are readiness probes.
They must not run a private blocking loop. `run(timeoutms)` pumps the provider's
reactor, and the public facade exposes pumping as `io.net.pump`. Keep handle
ownership separate for listeners, connect requests, streams, and datagrams.

Pending and EOF conventions differ by operation and are documented below. Report
failures through the declared error result rather than disguising them as
pending work. A TLS provider wrapping these streams must understand their handle
representation; selection cannot make unrelated transport handles interoperable.

## TLS

`TlsProvider` wraps network streams with TLS.

The build binds the TLS implementation together with its network transport.
The facade retains it and supplies its explicit receiver. The implementation
wraps an opaque network stream handle, so both must use the same transport
representation.

Wrapping creates TLS state; handshake and I/O then report pending work to the
facade, which drives readiness. Verification is a policy input and an observable
session result. Do not report a verified peer merely because a handshake
completed with verification disabled. ALPN protocol text describes the negotiated
result; resumed is an optional observation.

closenotify sends the TLS shutdown notification and may need further progress.
destroy releases session state and the transport it owns. No method may resolve
or switch providers.
]]
module io.net.internal.contracts

local source1 = require("nupp.io.net.contracts")
export type Provider = source1.Provider

--- A TLS provider wrapping compatible network handles.
export interface TlsProvider

    --- Creates session state over a compatible network handle. The provider
    --- consumes the handle on success and failure.
    ---
    --- Certificate, private key, authority, hostname, and ALPN options follow
    --- the public TLS API. Returns the session or nil and an error.
    @readonly wrap: function(
        self: Provider,
        handle: any,
        server: boolean,
        hostname: string,
        certificate: string,
        privatekey: string,
        authority: string?,
        protocols: string,
        verify: boolean
    ): (any?, string?)

    --- Returns true when ready, false while pending, or nil and an error.
    @readonly handshake: function(self: Provider, session: any): (boolean?, string?)

    --- Reports whether peer verification succeeded for this session.
    @readonly verified: function(self: Provider, session: any): boolean

    --- Optionally reports whether this session resumed prior TLS state.
    @readonly resumed: (function(self: TlsProvider, session: any): boolean)?

    --- Returns at most `wanted` bytes, nil while pending, an empty string at
    --- EOF, or nil and an error.
    @readonly read: function(self: Provider, session: any, wanted: integer): (string?, string?)

    --- Returns a positive byte count no greater than the input length, nil
    --- while pending, or nil and an error.
    @readonly write: function(self: Provider, session: any, bytes: string): (integer?, string?)

    --- Returns true when encrypted output has drained, false while pending,
    --- or false with an error on failure.
    @readonly flushed: function(self: Provider, session: any): (boolean, string?)

    --- Starts or continues orderly TLS shutdown; true means complete, or that
    --- the bounded time a drain may take is spent, and false means pending
    --- unless accompanied by an error.
    @readonly closenotify: function(self: Provider, session: any): (boolean, string?)

    --- Releases TLS session state and its owned transport.
    @readonly destroy: function(self: Provider, session: any): nil

    --- Reports whether the session remains connected.
    @readonly connected: function(self: Provider, session: any): boolean

    --- Returns the negotiated ALPN protocol, or nil when none is available.
    @readonly protocol: function(self: Provider, session: any): string?

end
